cd - will take you back one directory
current user echo $USER, home directory echo $HOME, shell echo $SHELL, you can also use the env command to check enviroement variables.
ls -la for permissions and ownerships, ls -li for index numbers so you can find things quickly, or do both. to cite a index number to a file use "find / inum 'index number'"
